# graphify. The graph itself is tracked, because `query`, `path`, `explain` and
# `affected` have nothing to read without it, and a container that comes up
# without one gives those commands an empty answer rather than an error — which
# is the worse failure of the two.
#
# What stays out is everything derived from it: the 2.5 MB interactive viz, the
# extractor's cache, the input-hash manifest, the community-label sidecar and
# the dated backups `update` leaves behind. All of those come back from
# `graphify update .`, which needs no API key.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!graphify-out/graph.json

# Local build configuration overriding config/get-teksi.json
config/local.json

# Report of keys with no translation yet — regenerated on every build.
l10n-untranslated.json
